pvs_cad: THEORY
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Everything (cad), (cad *), (cad-direct), (cad :cad-only? t) and (cad-qe)
% need in one import, except what pins down constants and functions of
% constants (pi, sin(x) after skeep: IMPORTING pvs_cad_num instead, which
% adds trans_bounds and NASALib's interval_arith@strategies): IMPORTING
% pvs_cad makes them available,
% deciding through the Collins run (cad_decide8, qe8) and taking formulas of
% any shape (grouped binders and a goal NOT A need nothing more; quantifiers
% inside connectives, binders over posreal / nnreal / negreal / npreal /
% nzreal, and other real terms in a formula given to (cad), need gform_ok).
% See cad_showcase.
% It does not import every theorem of the library: col_line (col_cells),
% col_found_ok (col_found_cad), decb_run (decb_cad_run), cad_sa (the cells
% quantifier-free definable) and qelim_ok are outside its import closure --
% import those.
%----------------------------------------------------------------------------
BEGIN
  IMPORTING cad_decide8, qe8, gform_ok, mpoly_embed, cad_endgame
END pvs_cad
